\s1 King David's ancestors
\rem /s1 The Family Tree of King David; From Judah's Grandson Hezron to David
\p
\v 9 Hetsron¦187693 had three sons¦187692: Yerahme'el¦187700, Ram¦187703, and¦187692 Keluvay¦187706.\f + \fr 2:9 \ft In the Hebrew, ‘Keluvay’ is called ‘Kalev’ (Caleb) below.\f*
\rem /s2 From Ram Son of Hezron
\p
\v 10 Ram¦187708 was the father¦187709 of Amminadav¦187712, and¦187713 Amminadav¦187713 was the father¦187714 of Nahshon¦187717—a leader¦187718 of¦187718 the¦187719 \add ≈tribe\add* of¦187719 Yehudah¦187720.
\v 11 Nahshon¦187722 was the father¦187723 of Salma¦187726. Salma¦187727 was the father¦187728 of Boaz¦187731.
\v 12 Boaz¦187733 was the father¦187734 of Oved. Oved was the father¦187739 of Yishay¦187742 \add !(Jesse¦187742)\add*.
\v 13 Yishay¦187744 had his¦187748 son Eliav¦187751 first¦187748, Abinadab¦187752 second¦187753, Shimea¦187754 third¦187755.
\v 14 Netanel fourth¦187758, Raddai¦187759 fifth¦187760,
\v 15 Otsem sixth¦187763, then David¦187764 \add ≈last\add*.
\v 16 Their¦187767 sisters¦187767 were¦187769 Tseruyah¦187772 and Avigayil¦187770. Tseruyah's¦187769 three¦187778 sons¦187771 were¦187773 Avshai¦187774, Yoav¦187774 \add !(Joab¦187774)\add*, and¦187775 Asah'el.
\v 17 Avigayil had Amasa¦187786. Amasa's¦187784 father¦187785 was¦187787 Yeter¦187787, a descendant of¦187785 Yishmael¦187788 \add !(Ishmael¦187788)\add*.
\s1 The descendants of Kalev (Caleb)
