\rem /s2 Caleb Son of Hezron
\p
\v 18 Hetsron's¦187793 \add third\add* son¦187791 Kalev \add !(Caleb)\add* had sons with¦187795 Azuvah¦187797, one of¦187803 his wives. The sons were¦187803 Yesher¦187804, Shovav¦187805, and¦187790 Ardon¦187806. (The other wife's¦187798 name was¦187803 Yeriot.)
\v 19 When¦187808 Azuvah¦187809 died¦187808, Kalev¦187813 married Efrat¦187816, and¦187808 they had a son named Hur¦187821.
\v 20 Hur¦187823 was the father¦187824 of Uri¦187827, and¦187828 Uri¦187828 was the father¦187829 of Betsal'el.
\p
\v 21 Later¦187835, when Hetsron was¦187848 sixty¦187850 years¦187851 old, he¦187836 \add ≈had¦187846 sexual intercourse\add* with a daughter¦187840 of¦187840 Makir¦187842 from the¦187843 region of¦187843 Gilead¦187844 and¦187845 married¦187846 her¦187846. \add @Hetsron's¦187837 new¦187837 wife¦187837\add* gave¦187852 birth¦187852 to¦187853 \add their son\add* Seguv¦187856.
\v 22 Seguv was¦187863 the father¦187859 of¦187870 Yair, and¦187858 Yair¦187862 controlled twenty-three¦187866 cities¦187868 in¦187869 the¦187870 Gilead¦187870 region¦187869.
\v 23 \add ≈But¦187872\add* Geshur¦187873 and¦187875 Aram¦187875 captured¦187872 Havvot-Yair¦187879 and Kenat¦187883 from¦187880 them¦187880, plus¦187875 \add ≈their surrounding towns\add*—sixty¦187887 towns \add in all,\add* \add ≈populated by\add* descendants¦187892 of¦187892 Makir¦187893 (the¦187892 father¦187894 of¦187894 Gilead¦187896).
\v 24 After¦187898 Hetsron's¦187901 death¦187899 in¦187902 Kalev¦187902-Efratah¦187903, his wife¦187904 Aviyyah gave¦187907 birth¦187907 to¦187908 his son Ashhur¦187911, the¦187912 father¦187912 of¦187912 Tekoa¦187913.
\s1 Yerahme'el's descendants
\rem /s1 Descendants of Hezron's Son Jerahmeel; The Descendants of Jerahmeel
\rem /s2 Jerahmeel Son of Hezron
\p
\v 25 Hetsron's¦187920 oldest son¦187916 was¦187915 Yerahme'el¦187918 \add and\add* his sons¦187916 were¦187915 Ram¦187923 (the¦187916 oldest), Bunah¦187924, Oren¦187925, Otsem¦187926, and Ahiyah¦187927.
\v 26 Yerahme'el¦187932 had another¦187931 wife¦187930 named¦187933 Atarah¦187934. She¦187935 was¦187936 the¦187936 mother¦187936 of¦187936 Onam¦187937.
\v 27 The¦187941 sons¦187941 of¦187941 Yerahme'el's¦187945 oldest son¦187941, Ram¦187943, were¦187940 Maats¦187946, Yamin¦187947, and¦187940 Eker¦187948.
\v 28 Onam's¦187953 sons were Shammai¦187957 and Yada¦187955, and Shammai's¦187954 sons were¦187958 Nadav¦187958 and¦187959 Avishur¦187959.
\p
\v 29 Avishur's¦187963 wife¦187962 was¦187964 Avihayil¦187964, and \add ≈their sons were¦187964\add* Ahban¦187969 and¦187970 Molid¦187972.
\v 30 Nadav's¦187975 sons¦187974 were¦187976 Seled and¦187974 Appayim¦187977. (Seled¦187979 died¦187978 childless.)
\v 31 Appayim's¦187985 son was¦187986 Yishi¦187986, Yishi's¦187988 son was¦187989 Sheshan¦187991, and¦187990 Sheshan's¦187989 son¦187990 was¦187992 Ahlai¦187992.
\p
\v 32 The¦187994 sons¦187994 of¦187995 Shammai's¦187997 brother¦187996 Yada¦187995 were¦187998 Yeter and¦187994 Yonatan¦187999. (Yeter¦188001 died¦188000 childless.)
\v 33 Yonatan's¦188007 sons¦188006 were¦188008 Pelet¦188008 and¦188009 Zaza¦188009.
\m Those were¦188011 the¦188012 descendants of¦188012 Yerahme'el.
\p
\v 34 Sheshan¦188018 had no sons¦188019, only daughters¦188023. He¦188024 had a¦188025 \add male\add* servant¦188025 from¦188026 Egypt¦188026 whose name¦188027 was¦188028 Yarha¦188028,
\v 35 and¦188030 Sheshan¦188031 gave¦188030 his¦188034 daughter¦188034 to¦188035 \add *him¦188039\add* for¦188037 a wife¦188037, and¦188038 \add ≈they had a son\add* Attai¦188042.
\v 36 Attai was the father¦188045 of Natan¦188048, and¦188049 Natan¦188049 was the father¦188050 of Zavad¦188053.
\v 37 Zavad was the father¦188056 of Eflal¦188059, and¦188060 Eflal¦188060 was the father¦188061 of Oved¦188064.
\v 38 Oved was the father¦188067 of Yehu¦188070, and¦188071 Yehu¦188071 was the father¦188072 of Azaryah¦188075.
\v 39 Azaryah¦188077 was the father¦188078 of Helets, and¦188082 Helets was the father¦188083 of Eleasah¦188086.
\v 40 Eleasah was the father¦188089 of Sismai¦188092, and¦188093 Sismai¦188093 was the father¦188094 of Shallum¦188097.
\v 41 Shallum¦188099 was the father¦188100 of Yekamyah, and¦188104 Yekamyah was the father¦188105 of Elishama¦188108.
\s1 The other descendants of Kalev
