\p
\v 36 Zofah's¦191111 sons¦191110 were¦191112 Suah¦191112, Harnefer¦191113, Shual¦191114, Beri¦191115, Yimrah¦191116,
\v 37 Betser, Hod¦191119, Shamma¦191120, Shilshah¦191121, Yitran¦191122 (whose other name was Yeter), and¦191119 Beera¦191123.
\p
\v 38 Yeter's¦191126 sons¦191125 were¦191127 Yefunneh¦191127, Pispah¦191128, and¦191125 Ara¦191129.
\v 39 \add Another of Asher's descendants was\add* Ulla¦191132, whose sons¦191131 were¦191133 Arah¦191133, Hanniel¦191134, and¦191131 Ritsia.
\p
\v 40 All¦191137 those¦191139 were¦191140 Asher's¦191142 descendants¦191140, \add ≈clan leaders\add*, chosen¦191147, very strong¦191148, \add ≈leaders of¦191140 leaders¦191151\add*. And¦191152 there were¦191156 26,000 men¦191156 listed in their¦191152 genealogy¦191152 in the¦191140 army¦191153.
\c 8
