\p
\v 1 Benyamin¦191162 had sons: Bela¦191166, Ashbel¦191168, Aharah¦191170,
\v 2 Nohah¦191173, and¦191175 the¦191174 fifth¦191176, Rafa¦191175.
\p
\v 3 Bela's¦191181 sons¦191180 were¦191179 Addar¦191182, Gera¦191183, Abihud¦191184,
\v 4 Avishua, Naaman¦191187, Ahoah¦191188,
\v 5 Gera, Shefufan, and¦191190 Huram¦191192.
\p
\v 6 \add One of Gera's sons was\add* Ehud¦191196. \add ≈His descendants¦191195 were¦191199 leaders of their clans who lived¦191201\add* in Geba¦191202 \add city\add*, but¦191194 were¦191195 taken¦191203 into¦191203 exile¦191203 to¦191204 Manahat¦191206.
\v 7 Ehud's sons were Naaman, Ahiyah¦191209, and¦191210 Gera. Gera \add ≈was the one who led¦191212 them¦191212\add* \add when they moved to Manahat\add*. He¦191213 \add ≈was the father¦191213 of\add* Uzza¦191216 and¦191217 Ahihud¦191219.
\p
\v 8 \add Another of Benyamin's descendants was\add* Shaharayim¦191221, \add ≈who lived\add* in¦191223 the¦191223 Moav¦191224 countryside¦191223. He¦191227 \add ≈divorced\add* his¦191233 wives¦191233 Hushim¦191229 and¦191230 Baara¦191232,
\v 9 and¦191235 fathered¦191235 \add sons\add* with his¦191239 wife¦191239 Hodesh¦191238: Yobab¦191242, Tsivya¦191245, Mesha¦191248, Malkam¦191251,
\v 10 Yeuts, Sakeya, and¦191253 Mirmah¦191261. They all became leaders of¦191263 their clans.
\v 11 (He'd fathered¦191268 Avituv¦191271 and¦191272 Elpaal¦191274 by Hushim.)
\p
\v 12 Elpaal's¦191277 sons¦191276 were¦191278 Eber¦191278, Misham¦191279, Shemed¦191280 (who built¦191282 Ono¦191285 \add city\add*, plus¦191279 Lod¦191288 and¦191276 its¦191289 towns¦191289),
