\p
\v 29 \add Another of Benyamin's descendants was Yeiel\add*—he \add ≈was a founder¦191384 of\add* Gibeon¦191382 \add city\add*. His¦191387 wife¦191387 was¦191388 Maakah¦191388.
\v 30 His¦191390 sons¦191390, \add starting with\add* the¦191391 eldest¦191391, were¦191392 Avdon¦191392, Tsur¦191393, Kish¦191394, Baal¦191395, Nadav¦191396,
\v 31 Gedor, Ahyo¦191399, and¦191398 Zeker¦191400.
\v 32 Miklot \add (another of Yeiel's sons)\add* was Shimeah's¦191406 father¦191403. All those descendants of Yeiel also¦191407 lived¦191412 in¦191413 Yerushalem¦191413 near their¦191416 relatives¦191411.
\s1 The descendants of King Shaul (Saul)
\rem /s1 The Family of King Saul
\p
\v 33 Ner¦191419 was the father¦191420 of Kish. Kish was the father¦191425 of \add King\add* Shaul¦191428. Shaul¦191429 was the father¦191430 of Yonatan¦191433 \add !(Jonathan¦191433)\add*, Malki¦191436-Shua¦191438, Avinadav¦191441, and¦191434 Esh-Baal.
\v 34 Yonatan's¦191448 son¦191446 was Meriv-Baal. Meriv-Baal was the¦191446 father¦191453 of¦191446 Mikah¦191456.
\p
