\v 36 Ahaz¦191466 was the father¦191467 of Yehoaddah. Yehoaddah was the father¦191472 of Alemet¦191475, Azmavet¦191478, and¦191466 Zimri¦191481. Zimri¦191482 was the father¦191483 of Motsa¦191486.
\v 37 Motsa was the father¦191489 of¦191494 Binea. Rafah was Binea's¦191492 son. Eleasah was Rafah's¦191493 son. Atsel¦191497 was Eleasah's¦191495 son.
\p
\v 38 Atsel¦191516 had \add ≈a total¦191512 of¦191504\add* six¦191501 sons¦191515, named¦191504 Azrikam¦191505, Bokeru, Yishmael¦191508, Shearyah¦191509, Ovadyah¦191510, and¦191500 Hanan¦191511.
\v 39 Atsel had a brother¦191520, Eshek. Eshek's¦191519 oldest son¦191518 was¦191521 Ulam¦191521. His¦191522 other sons¦191518 were¦191523 Yeush¦191523 and¦191525 Elifelet¦191525.
\p
\v 40 Ulam's¦191531 sons were powerful¦191533 warriors¦191532 who¦191536 were also¦191538 archers. Altogether they¦191528 had¦191538 150 sons and¦191528 grandsons.
\p All¦191544 those¦191546 were¦191528 Benyamin's¦191548 descendants.
\c 9
\s1 Those who returned from captivity
\rem /s1 The restored community; The People Who Returned from Captivity
\p
\v 1 \add ≈So the genealogy of all¦191551 Israelis¦191560 was listed¦191554\add*—yes, written¦191556 on¦191565 the scroll¦191559 of Yisrael's¦191553 kings¦191560.
\rem /s1 The Returning Exiles; The People in Jerusalem
\p Then¦191562 Yehudah¦191562 \add !(Judah¦191562)\add* was¦191563 taken¦191563 into¦191563 exile¦191563 to¦191564 Babylon¦191564 because of¦191559 their¦191565 unfaithfulness¦191565.
\v 2 The¦191568 first¦191569 \add ≈to return and resettle their land and\add* their cities¦191572 were¦191573 \add some\add* priests¦191574, Levites¦191575, temple¦191576 servants¦191576, and \add other\add* Israelis¦191573.\x + \xo 9:2-3: \xt Ezr 2:27; Neh 7:73.\x*
\rem /s1 Inhabitants of Jerusalem after the Exile
\v 3 \add Some from the tribes of\add* Yehudah¦191583, Benyamin¦191587, Efrayim¦191591, and¦191592 Menashsheh¦191592 \add also returned and\add* lived¦191579 in¦191578 Yerushalem, \add including the following:\add*
\p
\v 4 Utai son¦191595 of¦191595 Ammihud (Ammihud was Omri's¦191600 son¦191601, Omri was Imri's¦191603 son, Imri was Bani's son, Bani was a descendant¦191609 of Perets, Perets was Yehudah's¦191614 son),
\v 5 Asayah¦191619 and¦191621 his¦191621 sons¦191621 (descendants¦191621 of¦191621 Shilon—Asayah was the¦191618 oldest¦191620),
\v 6 and Yeuel¦191628 and¦191623 690 other relatives¦191629 from¦191623 Zerah's¦191627 clan.
\p
\v 7 From¦191635 Benyamin's¦191638 descendants¦191637, Sallu¦191639 (who was Meshullam's¦191642 son¦191643, Meshullam was Hodavyah's¦191645 son¦191646, Hodavyah was Hassenuah's¦191648 son),
\v 8 Ibneyah (Yeroham's¦191653 son), Elah¦191654 (who was Uzzi's¦191657 son¦191658, Uzzi was Mikri's¦191660 son), and¦191650 Meshullam¦191661 (who was Shefatyah's¦191664 son¦191665, Shefatyah was Reuel's¦191667 son¦191668, Reuel was Yivniyah's¦191670 son).
\p
\v 9 In all¦191678, there were 956 of Benyamin's descendants¦191673 living in Yerushalem. All¦191678 those¦191680 \add above\add* were leaders of their¦191672 clans.
\rem /s1 The Returning Priests; Priestly Families; The Priests Who Lived in Jerusalem
\p
\v 10 Some of the¦191690 priests¦191690 \add who returned to Yehudah\add* were: Yedayah¦191691, Yehoyariv¦191692, Yakin¦191693,
\v 11 Azaryah¦191695, the leading official at the temple¦191712 (Azaryah was Hilkiyah's¦191698 son¦191699, Hilkiyah was Meshullam's¦191701 son¦191702, Meshullam was Tsadok's¦191704 son¦191705, Tsadok was Merayot's¦191707 son¦191708, Merayot was Ahituv's¦191710 son),
\v 12 Adayah¦191716 (who was Yeroham's¦191719 son¦191720, Yeroham was Pashhur's¦191722 son¦191723, Pashhur was Malkiyah's¦191725 son), and¦191726 Maasai¦191726 (who was Adiel's¦191729 son¦191730, Adiel was Yahzerah's¦191732 son¦191733, Yahzerah was Meshullam's¦191735 son¦191736, Meshullam was Meshillemit's¦191738 son¦191739, Meshillemit was Immer's¦191741 son).
\p
\v 13 Altogether there were 1,760 \add priests who returned to Yehudah\add*. \add ≈They were leaders of¦191743 their¦191743 clans, and¦191748 they were all capable and¦191750 responsible\add* to work¦191754 in God's residence.
\s1 Levites who returned
\rem /s1 The Returning Levites; Levitical Families; The Levites Who Lived in Jerusalem
\p
\v 14 From¦191759 Levi's descendants¦191774 \add who returned to Yehudah there were\add*: Shemayah¦191762 (who was Hasshuv's son, Hasshuv was Azrikam's¦191768 son¦191769, Azrikam was Hashavyah's¦191771 son, Hashavyah was a descendant¦191774 of¦191769 \add Levi's youngest son\add* Merari¦191775),
\rem /s1 The Temple Guards Who Lived in Jerusalem
\v 15 Bakbakkar, Heresh¦191778, Galal¦191779, Mattanyah¦191780 (who was Mika's son, Mika was Zikri's¦191786 son¦191787, Zikri was Asaf's¦191789 son),
\v 16 Ovadyah (who was Shemayah's¦191794 son¦191795, Shemayah was Galal's¦191797 son¦191798, Galal was Yedutun's¦191800 son), and¦191791 Berekyah¦191801 who¦191808 lived in¦191809 one of¦191798 the villages¦191809 where the Netofat people lived (Berekyah was Asa's¦191804 son¦191805, Asa was Elkanah's¦191807 son).
\p
\v 17 From Levi's descendants who returned to Yehudah and who guarded the¦191812 temple gates there were¦191813 Shallum¦191813, Akkuv¦191814, Talmon¦191815, Ahiman¦191816, and¦191812 some of¦191817 their relatives¦191817. Shallum¦191818 was¦191819 their leader¦191819.
\v 18 Those descendents¦191830 of¦191824 Levi¦191831 were¦191828 gatekeepers¦191828 at the King's¦191825 Gate¦191824 on¦191824 the east¦191826, \add ≈and¦191821 their descendants¦191830 still are¦191828, even to this day\add*.
\p
\v 19 Shallum¦191833 was Kore's¦191836 son, Kore¦191842 was Evyasaf's¦191839 son, and Evyasaf was Korah's son. Shallum and his relatives¦191843 from his clan (Korah's descendants) had the¦191857 duty of¦191857 being gatekeepers, responsible for guarding the entrances¦191860 to Yahweh's¦191858 temple¦191844, as their¦191854 ancestors¦191854 had done.
\v 20 \add ≈Previously\add* Pinehas (Eleazar's¦191865 son¦191863) \add ≈had¦191867 supervised\add* the¦191863 gatekeepers. Yahweh¦191870 was¦191867 with¦191872 \add @Pinehas¦191872\add*.
\p
\v 21 Zekaryah (Meshelemyah's¦191876 son¦191875) was¦191877 gatekeeper¦191877 of¦191875 the¦191878 entrance¦191878 to the¦191879 assembly tent¦191879.
\v 22 \add ≈Altogether, there were¦191883 212 men chosen¦191883 to¦191884 guard the gates\add*. \add ≈The¦191896 records¦191891 of¦191890 the clans in¦191885 their villages¦191890 listed their names\add*. \add King\add* David¦191894 and¦191895 \add ≈the prophet¦191896\add* Shemuel¦191895 \add !(Samuel¦191895)\add* \add ≈appointed¦191893 them¦191882 because they¦191889 were¦191890 dependable\add*.
\v 23 They¦191899 and¦191899 their¦191900 sons \add watched\add* over¦191901 the¦191903 gates¦191903 of¦191906 Yahweh's¦191906 house¦191907, that is¦191901, the \add ≈sacred\add* tent¦191909, as guards¦191910.
\v 24 There were¦191914 gatekeepers¦191915 on each of the¦191915 \add temple's\add* four¦191912 sides¦191913: east¦191916, west¦191917, north¦191918, and¦191919 south¦191919.
\v 25 Their¦191921 relatives¦191921 in¦191922 their¦191922 villages¦191922 would come¦191923 in from¦191926 time to time \add to relieve them\add* for¦191924 seven¦191924 days¦191925,
\v 26 because¦191934 the¦191937 four¦191937 leaders of¦191937 the gatekeepers¦191939 were¦191941 Levites¦191941, and¦191942 they¦191942 were \add also\add* \add ≈trusted¦191935 to supervise\add* the rooms¦191945 and¦191946 the¦191947 treasuries¦191947 in¦191935 God's¦191949 residence.
\v 27 They¦191954 would \add ≈spend¦191955 the¦191955 night¦191955\add* around¦191951 the¦191952 \add ≈temple¦191952\add* while they¦191955 were¦191961 in charge, and¦191951 \add ≈would open it with the key¦191963 each\add* morning¦191964.
\rem /s1 The Other Levites
\p
\v 28 Some¦191967 of¦191967 them¦191967 \add ≈monitored the¦191970 utensils¦191970 used in¦191974 the activities\add*—counting them as they¦191975 brought¦191975 them¦191975 out¦191977 and¦191976 \add ≈when they¦191977 put them¦191977 away\add* \add again\add*.
\v 29 \add ≈Others\add* took care of¦191979 the¦191983 containers and¦191984 utensils¦191987 used in the¦191988 sanctuary¦191988, along with the¦191991 fine¦191991 flour¦191991, the¦191992 wine¦191992 and¦191993 oil¦191993, and¦191994 the¦191994 frankincense¦191994 and¦191995 spices¦191995.
\v 30 Some of¦191999 the¦192000 priests¦192000 mixed¦192001 \add the fragrances and\add* spices¦192003.
\p
\v 31 There was a Levite¦192008 \add named\add* Mattityah¦192005 (Shallum's¦192011 oldest son, who was a descendant of Korah) whose official duty \add ≈was supervising the¦192015 baking of¦192015 the¦192016 flat¦192016 breads\add*.
\v 32 Some¦192022 of Kohat's¦192021 descendants¦192020 prepared¦192029 the rows¦192028 of bread¦192027 to¦192029 \add be laid out on the sacred table\add* every rest day.
\p
\v 33 Some of Levi's descendants were¦192039 \add temple musicians and\add* singers¦192035. The¦192035 leaders of those¦192034 families stayed in¦192039 the¦192036 temple accommodations. They \add ≈didn't have other duties¦192040,\add* because¦192042 they¦192046 \add were expected to\add* serve day¦192044 and¦192045 night¦192045.
\v 34 Those were¦192050 the¦192050 heads¦192050 of¦192050 the¦192051 Levite¦192052 \add ≈families¦192051\add* according¦192053 to¦192053 their¦192053 generations¦192053, \add and\add* they¦192056 lived¦192056 in¦192057 Yerushalem¦192057.
\s1 King Shaul's ancestors and descendants
\rem /s1 The Ancestors and Descendants of King Saul; The Genealogy of Saul; King Saul's Family Tree; The Family of King Saul
\r (1 Chr. 8:29-38)
\p
\v 35 \add Another of Benyamin's descendants was\add* Yeiel¦192065. He was \add ≈a founder¦192062\add* of Gibeon¦192060 \add city\add* and¦192067 lived¦192061 there. His¦192068 wife¦192068 was¦192069 Maakah¦192069.
\v 36 His¦192071 oldest son¦192071 was¦192073 Avdon¦192073, and¦192071 his¦192071 other sons¦192071 were¦192073 Tsur¦192074, Kish¦192075, Baal¦192076, Ner¦192077, Nadav¦192078,
\v 37 Gedor, Ahyo¦192081, Zekaryah¦192082, and¦192080 Miklot¦192083.
\v 38 Miklot was Shimeam's father¦192086. They¦192092 also¦192090 lived¦192095 \add ≈near\add* their¦192094 relatives¦192099 in¦192096 Yerushalem¦192096.
\p
\v 39 Ner¦192102 was the father¦192103 of Kish. Kish was the father¦192108 of \add King\add* Shaul \add !(Saul¦192111)\add*. Shaul¦192112 was the father¦192113 of Yonatan¦192116 \add !(Jonathan¦192116)\add*, Malki¦192119-Shua¦192121, Avinadav¦192124, and¦192117 Esh-Baal.
\v 40 Yonatan's¦192131 son¦192129 was Meriv-Baal. Meriv-Baal was the¦192129 father¦192137 of¦192129 Mikah¦192140.
\v 41 Mikah's¦192143 sons¦192142 were¦192144 Piton¦192144, Melek¦192145, and¦192142 Tahrea¦192146.
\v 42 Ahaz¦192148 was the father¦192149 of Yarah¦192152. Yarah¦192153 was the father¦192154 of Alemet¦192157, Azmavet¦192160, and¦192148 Zimri¦192163. Zimri¦192164 was the father¦192165 of Motsa¦192168.
\v 43 Motsa was the father¦192171 of¦192176 Binea. Refayah was Binea's¦192174 son. Eleasah was Refayah's¦192175 son. Atsel¦192179 was Eleasah's¦192177 son.
\p
\v 44 Atsel¦192196 had six¦192183 sons¦192184, named¦192186 Azrikam¦192187, Bokeru, Yishmael¦192190, Shearyah¦192191, Ovadyah¦192192, and¦192182 Hanan¦192193.
\c 10
\s1 The death of King Shaul and his sons
\rem /s1 David succeeds Saul; Saul Takes His Life; Death of Saul and His Sons; The Death of King Saul
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Sam. 31:1-13)
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* the¦192199 Philistines fought¦192200 against¦192201 Yisrael¦192201, and¦192202 the¦192203 Israeli¦192205 men¦192203 fled¦192202 \add ≈away\add* from¦192206 the¦192207 Philistines, and¦192208 \add ≈many were killed¦192209\add* on¦192201 Mt¦192210. Gilboa¦192211.
\v 2 Then¦192213 the¦192214 Philistines¦192214 pursued¦192213 Shaul¦192216 and¦192217 his sons, and¦192219 \add *they¦192219\add* \add ≈killed¦192219\add* \add his\add* sons Yonatan¦192223, Avinadav¦192226, and¦192227 Malki¦192229-Shua¦192231.
\v 3 The¦192236 battle¦192236 against Shaul¦192239 was¦192243 very fierce, \add ≈and¦192235 then¦192235\add* the¦192246 archers¦192246 spotted him and¦192235 wounded¦192243 him.
\v 4 Then¦192248 Shaul¦192249 said¦192248 to¦192250 his equipment carrier, “Draw¦192254 your¦192255 sword and¦192257 pierce¦192257 me¦192257 with¦192258 it¦192258, so those¦192263 uncircumcised¦192262 \add Philistines\add* \add ^can't come¦192261 here\add* and torture me.” But¦192248 his equipment carrier was¦192268 very¦192273 scared and wasn't willing¦192268 to do it, so Shaul took¦192275 \add &his¦192279\add* sword¦192279 and¦192280 fell¦192280 onto it¦192281.
