\v 18 \add ≈But¦196437 the Arameans¦196438 fled¦196437 away from¦196439 the Israelis¦196440\add*, and¦196441 David¦196442 killed¦196441 seven¦196444 thousand¦196445 chariot¦196446 \add drivers\add* and¦196447 forty¦196447 thousand¦196448 men¦196449 on¦196450 foot¦196450, as well as killing Shofak¦196452, their army¦196455 commander¦196453.
\v 19 When¦196458 Hadadezer's¦196460 servants¦196459 saw¦196458 that¦196461 \add ≈Yisrael¦196464 had¦196462 defeated¦196462 them\add*, they¦196458 made¦196465 peace¦196465 with¦196466 David¦196468 and¦196458 \add ≈became¦196469 his subjects¦196469, so\add* Aram¦196473 \add !(Syria¦196473)\add* wasn't willing¦196472 to¦196474 help¦196474 the¦196477 Ammonites¦196479 \add militarily\add* any more.
