\p
\v 1 Then a trouble-maker worked against Yisrael¦196672 \add ≈by\add* encouraging David¦196676 \add ≈to¦196677 take a census of\add* Yisrael¦196680,
\v 2 \add ≈so¦196682\add* David¦196683 \add ≈ordered¦196682\add* Yoav¦196686 and¦196687 \add ≈the other officials\add*, “Go¦196691 \add and\add* count¦196692 Yisrael¦196695 from¦196696 Be'er¦196696-Sheva \add in the south to all the way\add* as far \add north\add* as Dan¦196700, \add ≈then¦196682 come¦196691 and tell¦196682 me¦196702, so¦196703 that¦196703 I'll know¦196703 how many warriors I¦196703 have\add*.”
\p
\v 3 “My¦196720 master¦196720, the¦196721 king¦196721, may¦196710 Yahweh¦196720 \add ≈multiply his¦196714 people¦196714 one hundred¦196717 times¦196718 over\add*. Aren't they all¦196722 \add *your¦196723\add* servants¦196724?” Yoav¦196709 \add diplomatically\add* \add ≈queried\add*, “\add So\add* why does¦196726 my¦196720 master¦196723 \add ≈want¦196726 to¦196724 do¦196722\add* this¦196727? Why should¦196710 \add ≈he¦196708 bring judgement on\add* Yisrael¦196732?”
\v 4 \add ≈But¦196734 the king¦196736 insisted, so Yoav¦196740 was forced to go¦196741 and¦196734 gather statistics on the entire¦196744 country\add*. Then¦196734 he¦196741 returned¦196747 to Yerushalem¦196748
\v 5 and¦196750 \add ≈reported the¦196754 numbers¦196754\add* to¦196758 David¦196760. Yisrael¦196764 had 1.1 million sword-wielding¦196771 men¦196757, and Yehudah¦196772 had 470 thousand¦196766.
\v 6 \add ≈However,\add* \add @Yoav¦196794\add* had \add intentionally\add* not¦196783 counted¦196784 \add the tribes of\add* Levi and¦196782 Benyamin¦196782, because¦196786 \add *he¦196784\add* was¦196788 horrified by the¦196791 king's¦196791 command.
\s2 Punishment for the census
\rem /s1 Judgment for David's Sin
\p
\v 7 God \add ≈was¦196796 displeased¦196796 by what David had ordered, and¦196796 he¦196803 punished\add* Yisrael¦196806,
\v 8 and¦196809 David¦196810 said¦196809 to¦196811 God, “I've \add ≈disobeyed you badly by doing¦196817 that¦196821\add*. Please¦196825 \add ≈forgive your¦196829 servant¦196829 for¦196830 his disobedience\add*, because¦196830 I've \add ≈been very¦196815 stupid\add*.”
\p
\v 9 Then Yahweh¦196836 told¦196842 David's¦196841 prophet¦196840 Gad¦196839,
\v 10 “Go¦196844 and¦196845 tell¦196849 David¦196848 that Yahweh¦196852 says¦196851 this: \add ≈I'll give you three¦196853 options—choose¦196857 one¦196860 of¦196861 them¦196861 and¦196862 that's what I'll\add* do¦196862 to¦196864 you¦196864.”
\p
\v 11 \add ≈So¦196866\add* Gad¦196867 went¦196866 to¦196868 David¦196870 and¦196871 told¦196871 him¦196872, “Yahweh¦196876 says¦196875 that you must choose \add one of these punishments\add*:
\v 12 either three¦196883 years¦196884 of famine¦196885, or three¦196888 months¦196889 of being¦196890 overcome by your¦196893 enemies¦196895' \add ≈armies\add*, or three¦196900 days¦196901 of Yahweh's ‘sword¦196902’ of¦196902 pestilence¦196904 in¦196909 the¦196911 country¦196911 and¦196906 Yahweh's messenger¦196906 \add ≈bringing¦196917 destruction¦196908\add* across all¦196909 of¦196911 Yisrael's¦196912 territory¦196911. \add ≈So now¦196913, tell me what¦196915 answer I¦196917 should take¦196917\add* back¦196917 to¦196897 the one¦196920 who¦196920 sent¦196920 me¦196920.”
\p
\v 13 “\add Oh,\add* that's very distressing¦196929,” David¦196925 \add ≈replied¦196924\add* to¦196926 Gad¦196928, “but¦196924 please¦196935 don't¦196947 let me fall¦196933 into \add ≈my enemies'\add* hands¦196944. Yahweh¦196938 \add ≈is¦196929 very merciful, so please let¦196933 him be the¦196936 one to punish me¦196949 directly\add*.”
\p
\v 14 \add ≈So¦196951\add* Yahweh¦196952 \add ≈sent a¦196953 disease\add* throughout Yisrael¦196954, and¦196951 seventy¦196957 thousand¦196958 Israeli¦196956 men \add ≈died\add*.
\v 15 Then¦196961 God sent¦196961 a messenger¦196964 to destroy¦196967 Yerushalem¦196966, and¦196968 \add ≈while the disease was¦196968 still spreading,\add* Yahweh¦196983 \add ≈looked¦196969 down\add* and relented about¦196981 the tragedy, and he¦196975 told¦196975 the destroying¦196968 messenger¦196976, “Enough¦196978! Now \add ≈stop what you're doing\add*.” Now Yahweh's¦196970 messenger¦196982 \add happened to be\add* standing¦196984 at the¦196987 threshing¦196987 floor¦196987 belonging to Ornan¦196988 the¦196989 Yevusite.
\p
\v 16 \add As\add* David¦196993 \add ≈looked¦196997 up¦196992\add*, he¦196997 saw¦196997 Yahweh's¦197001 messenger¦197000 standing¦197002 between¦197003 the¦197004 earth¦197004 and¦197005 the¦197006 heavens¦197006, holding his¦197007 sword¦197007 stretched¦197010 out¦197010 over¦197011 Yerushalem¦197013. Then David¦197015 and the¦197016 elders¦197016, who were \add all\add* dressed in¦197018 sackcloth¦197018, fell¦197014 \add ≈to their knees and bowed their faces¦197021 to the ground¦197004\add*.
\v 17 Then¦197023 David¦197024 \add ≈asked¦197023\add* God¦197046, “Wasn't it¦197023 me myself who said¦197023 to¦197025 count¦197031 the¦197027 people? It's¦197023 me who \add ≈disobeyed and clearly did¦197030 what was¦197035 wrong¦197039\add*, but these¦197041 sheep¦197042, what¦197043 have¦197044 they¦197044 done¦197044? Yahweh¦197045 my god¦197046, please¦197048 \add ≈direct your punishment\add* against me¦197050 and¦197051 \add ≈my extended family¦197051\add*, but \add ≈don't¦197028 continue this\add* \add ≈deadly disease¦197055\add* on¦197032 your people¦197053.”
\rem /s1 David's Altar and Sacrifice; David Builds an Altar
\p
\v 18 Then Yahweh's¦197059 messenger¦197058 told¦197060 Gad¦197063 to tell¦197060 David¦197065 that¦197066 \add *he¦197068\add* should \add ≈build\add* an¦197071 altar¦197071 to¦197072 Yahweh¦197072 at¦197073 Ornan¦197074 the¦197073 Yevusite's threshing¦197073 floor¦197073.
\v 19 \add ≈So¦197077\add* David¦197078 went up \add to that place when he heard\add* \add ≈Gad's¦197081 message¦197079 that¦197082 was delivered\add* in¦197079 Yahweh's¦197085 name¦197084.
\v 20 \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* Ornan¦197088 was¦197096 threshing¦197098 wheat¦197099, and he turned¦197087 and¦197089 saw¦197089 \add Yahweh's\add* messenger¦197092, and he and his¦197094 four¦197093 sons¦197094 who were¦197096 with¦197095 him¦197095 \add quickly\add* hid¦197096 \add ≈behind something\add*.
\v 21 \add ≈When¦197101 David¦197102 arrived¦197101 there,\add* Ornan¦197105 saw¦197108 him and¦197112 left¦197112 the¦197115 threshing¦197115 floor¦197115 and¦197116 \add ≈knelt\add* in front¦197118 of David, bowing¦197116 his face¦197118 to¦197117 the ground¦197119.
\v 22 Then¦197121 David¦197122 \add ≈asked¦197121\add* Ornan¦197125, “Give¦197126 me¦197128 this place¦197129 with¦197136 its threshing¦197130 floor¦197130, and¦197121 I'll build¦197131 an¦197134 altar¦197134 to¦197135 Yahweh¦197135 on¦197136 it. \add ≈Sell it to me\add* at¦197136 the full¦197137 price¦197136, so¦197140 the¦197141 \add ≈deadly disease¦197141 affecting\add* the¦197143 people¦197143 will be¦197140 stopped¦197140.”
\p
\v 23 “My¦197154 master¦197154 the¦197155 king¦197155, take¦197150 \add ≈anything you want\add*,” Ornan¦197146 \add ≈replied¦197145\add*. “Listen, I'll donate the cattle for the burnt¦197161 offerings¦197161, and¦197162 the¦197162 threshing¦197162 sledges¦197162 for¦197163 firewood¦197163, and¦197164 the¦197164 wheat¦197164 for¦197165 the offering¦197165—all \add ≈at¦197157 no charge\add*.”
\p
\v 24 “No¦197173, I'll¦197177 most definitely pay¦197190 the¦197170 full¦197179 price¦197178,” King¦197170 David¦197171 \add ≈responded¦197169\add*. “I¦197183 couldn't offer¦197188 a burnt¦197189 offering¦197189 to¦197172 Yahweh¦197187 \add ≈if¦197174 it¦197169 hadn't cost me anything\add*.”
\v 25 \add ≈So¦197192\add* David¦197193 paid¦197192 Ornan¦197194 six¦197199 hundred¦197200 gold¦197197 pieces for¦197195 \add &his\add* place¦197195,
\v 26 and¦197202 he¦197202 built¦197202 an¦197205 altar to Yahweh there¦197203 and offered¦197221 burnt offerings and peace¦197209 offerings¦197209 on it¦197210. He¦197202 called¦197210 to¦197211 Yahweh, and¦197214 \add @Yahweh¦197214\add* answered¦197214 him¦197214 with¦197215 fire¦197215 from¦197216 the¦197218 heavens¦197218 on¦197219 that altar¦197220 with the¦197221 burnt¦197221 offering¦197221.
\p
\v 27 Then Yahweh¦197225 spoke¦197224 to¦197226 \add &his\add* messenger¦197226, who then returned¦197227 his sword¦197228 to his sheath¦197231.
\s1 The location for the future temple
