\p
\v 28 When¦197235 David¦197236 saw¦197235 that¦197237 Yahweh¦197240 had¦197239 answered¦197239 him¦197239 at¦197235 Ornan¦197242 the¦197234 Yevusite's¦197243 threshing¦197241 floor¦197241, he¦197244 sacrificed¦197244 there¦197245.
\v 29 \add ≈At¦197256 that time¦197256\add*, Yahweh's¦197248 \add sacred\add* tent¦197247 that¦197249 Mosheh¦197252 \add !(Moses¦197252)\add* had¦197251 made¦197251 in¦197253 the wilderness¦197253, and¦197254 the¦197254 altar¦197254 for burnt¦197255 sacrifices¦197255, were¦197258 \add ≈on¦197253 a hill used for worship near\add* Gibeon¦197259 \add city\add*.
\v 30 David¦197264 wasn't able¦197263 to¦197265 go¦197265 there to¦197267 \add ≈ask God's¦197268 direction\add* because¦197269 he¦197270 was¦197270 terrified¦197270 of¦197271 Yahweh's¦197274 messenger's¦197273 sword¦197272.
\c 22
\p
\v 1 Then David¦197278 said¦197277, “This¦197279 is¦197281 \add now\add* the¦197281 residence of¦197281 Yahweh¦197282 God, and¦197284 this¦197284 is¦197286 the¦197286 altar¦197286 for¦197287 Yisrael's¦197288 burnt¦197287 \add #offering¦197287\add*.”
\s1 The preparation of standing up of temple
\rem /s1 Preparations for the Temple; Preparation for the temple; Preparations for Building the Temple; David Prepares to Build the Temple
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 2 Then David¦197292 said¦197291 to¦197293 gather¦197293 the¦197296 foreigners who¦197297 \add ≈lived\add* in¦197298 Yisrael¦197299, and¦197300 he¦197300 assigned¦197300 \add ≈them the job of¦197299\add* hewing¦197304 out cut¦197302 stones¦197303 to¦197305 build¦197305 the residence¦197296 for God.
\v 3 He¦197317 prepared¦197316 a large quantity of¦197313 iron¦197309 for¦197315 the¦197313 door¦197313 \add ≈hinges and¦197309 fittings\add*, so much brass that it couldn't be¦197320 weighed¦197321,
\v 4 and¦197323 innumerable cedar¦197324 logs that the Tsidonians and the Tsorians \add !(Sidonians¦197329 and Tyrians¦197330)\add* brought¦197328 in¦197333 for David¦197334.
\v 5 David¦197338 said¦197337, “My¦197340 son¦197340 Shelomoh¦197339 \add !(Solomon¦197339)\add* is¦197341 young¦197340 and¦197342 not capable, and¦197343 the¦197343 house¦197343 to¦197344 be built¦197344 for¦197345 Yahweh¦197345 must¦197354 be \add ≈impressive for the¦197360 sake of his¦197361 reputation¦197349\add* and¦197350 honour¦197350 everywhere¦197351, \add so\add* I'll¦197354 prepare¦197354 for it¦197356 now.” \add ≈So\add* David¦197358 did a lot of preparation¦197357 before¦197360 \add ≈he¦197337 died¦197361\add*.
\rem /s1 David's Charge to Solomon and the Leaders
\p
\v 6 Then¦197363 David called¦197363 for his¦197365 son¦197365 Shelomoh¦197364 \add !(Solomon¦197364)\add*, and¦197366 ordered¦197366 him¦197366 to¦197364 build¦197367 a residence for¦197369 Yisrael's¦197371 god¦197370 Yahweh¦197369.
\v 7 David¦197375 told¦197374 \add *him\add*, “My¦197376 son¦197377, I¦197379 wanted to¦197384 build¦197384 a¦197385 temple¦197385 to honour my¦197388 god¦197388 Yahweh¦197387,\x + \xo 22:7-10: \xt 2Sam 7:1-16; 1Ch 17:1-14.\x*
\v 8 \add ≈but¦197390\add* Yahweh¦197394 \add ≈gave me this message¦197392\add*, ‘You've fought a lot of¦197392 battles¦197399 and¦197390 shed a large¦197400 amount of blood, \add so\add* you¦197401 won't¦197402 be¦197390 the¦197392 one who'll build¦197404 a residence \add ≈to¦197391 honour me¦197391\add*—you've¦197398 shed too much¦197409 blood on the ground¦197411 \add ≈in¦197397 my¦197412 sight¦197412\add*.’
\v 9 \add He told me,\add* ‘Listen, you'll have a son¦197416 who'll be a man¦197421 of¦197421 peace. I'll give¦197423 him¦197424 relief from¦197425 all¦197425 his enemies¦197427 from the surrounding regions. That's why he'll¦197420 be called¦197432 ‘Shelomoh¦197430’ \add (which sounds like ‘Shalom’—the Hebrew word for peace)\add*, and¦197433 I'll give peace¦197433 and¦197434 quietness¦197434 to¦197436 Yisrael¦197438 during¦197439 his lifetime¦197439.
\v 10 He'll¦197443 be the¦197456 one to¦197449 build¦197443 a¦197444 residence for¦197445 me¦197449, and he¦197443 himself will¦197447 become my¦197445 son¦197450, and¦197451 I'll become his father¦197454, and¦197455 I'll establish¦197455 his¦197457 kingdom's¦197457 \add ≈authority\add* over¦197458 Yisrael¦197460 forever¦197463.’
\p
\v 11 “Now¦197465, my¦197466 son¦197466, may¦197467 Yahweh be¦197467 with¦197469 you¦197469, and¦197470 may you¦197470 be¦197470 successful¦197470 and¦197471 build¦197471 a residence for Yahweh your¦197474 god¦197474, just¦197475 as¦197475 he¦197476 said¦197476 you¦197477 would.
\v 12 \add ≈I also¦197485 ask\add* Yahweh¦197494 to¦197482 give you¦197482 insight¦197484 and¦197485 understanding¦197485, and¦197486 give you charge¦197486 over¦197487 Yisrael¦197489 so that you can keep¦197490 your¦197495 god¦197495 Yahweh's¦197483 regulations.
\v 13 Then¦197497 you'll¦197498 succeed¦197498, if¦197499 you're careful¦197501 to follow the instructions¦197510 and the directions that¦197509 Yahweh¦197511 commanded¦197510 Mosheh¦197514 \add !(Moses¦197514)\add* concerning Yisrael¦197517. Be¦197518 strong¦197518 and¦197519 courageous¦197519. Don't¦197520 be¦197519 afraid¦197522 or discouraged¦197525.\x + \xo 22:13: \xt Josh 1:6-9.\x*
\p
\v 14 Now, see¦197527, \add ?≈despite many battles\add*, I've¦197529 prepared¦197529 the¦197530 following for¦197530 Yahweh's¦197532 residence: three thousand tonnes of gold¦197533 and thirty thousand tonnes of silver¦197538, along with¦197528 too much bronze¦197542 and¦197543 iron¦197543 to weigh¦197545, and¦197549 timber¦197549 and¦197550 \add cut\add* stones¦197550. Plus you'll¦197553 be able to add¦197553 more.
\v 15 \add ≈You'll have plenty of¦197557 skilled¦197565 workers, including¦197560 those who work with stone¦197561 and¦197555 those who work with wood¦197562\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈Then there's¦197574 so many skilled with gold¦197570 and silver¦197571, and¦197572 bronze¦197572 and¦197573 iron¦197573. So get organised and¦197577 get started\add*, and¦197578 may Yahweh¦197579 be¦197578 with¦197580 you¦197580.
\p
\v 17 Then¦197582 David¦197583 ordered¦197582 all¦197584 the¦197586 Israeli¦197586 officials¦197586 to¦197584 assist¦197588 his¦197590 son¦197590 Shelomoh¦197589, \add saying\add*,
\v 18 “Isn't Yahweh your god¦197594 with¦197595 you \add officials\add*, and¦197596 hasn't he¦197596 given¦197596 you peace \add ≈on every side\add*? He's¦197596 \add ≈allowed me to¦197597 take control of this region, and¦197606 this area has¦197606 been¦197606 subdued¦197606 with the¦197607 help\add* of¦197608 Yahweh and¦197610 his¦197611 people¦197611.
\v 19 Now¦197613, \add ≈dedicate your minds¦197615 and¦197616 strength to¦197617 requesting¦197617 advice from your god¦197619 Yahweh, then get organised and build¦197621 Yahweh God's sanctuary¦197624 so you can bring¦197627 the¦197630 box¦197630 containing Yahweh's agreement¦197631 to the residence to¦197637 be¦197638 built¦197638 to honour Yahweh's name¦197639, and bring God's sacred¦197635 items\add*.”
