\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 2 Then¦197657 \add @David¦197657\add* gathered¦197657 all¦197660 the¦197662 Israeli¦197663 officials and¦197664 the¦197664 priests¦197664 and¦197665 Levites¦197665.
\v 3 Counting¦197667 the¦197668 Levite¦197668 males that were thirty¦197670 years¦197671 old and¦197667 older, they¦197667 found there were¦197667 thirty-eight¦197677 thousand¦197679 men¦197676.
\v 4 \add David assigned\add* twenty-four¦197689 thousand of¦197685 them to supervise the¦197685 work¦197685 at Yahweh's¦197688 residence, six¦197694 thousand to be¦197692 officials¦197692 and¦197693 judges¦197693,
\v 5 four¦197697 thousand¦197698 to be¦197699 gatekeepers¦197699, and¦197697 four¦197700 thousand¦197701 to praise¦197707 Yahweh¦197703 using the musical instruments¦197704 that¦197705 he'd provided.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈So¦197709\add* David¦197710 divided¦197709 \add @the¦197713 Levites¦197713\add* into divisions¦197711 according¦197713 to¦197715 \add their ancestry through\add* Levi's¦197714 sons¦197713 Gershon¦197715, Kohat¦197716, and¦197717 Merari¦197717.
\s1 The Gershonites
\rem /s1 The Gershonites; Gershonites
\p
\v 7 The Gershonites \add included\add* Ladan¦197721 and¦197722 Shimei¦197722.
\v 8 Ladan's¦197726 three¦197731 sons¦197725 were¦197727: Yehiel¦197728 (the¦197727 oldest), Zetam¦197729, and¦197729 Yoel¦197730.
\v 9 Shimei's¦197735\f + \fr 23:9 \ft Possibly the wrong name got into the Hebrew here, because it disagrees with v10.\f* three¦197740 sons¦197734 were¦197736: Shelomot, Haziel¦197738, and¦197738 Haran¦197739. (They were¦197742 leaders of¦197742 Ladan's¦197744 clans.)
\v 10 Shimei's¦197748 four¦197757 sons¦197747 were¦197749: Yahat¦197749, Zina¦197750,\f + \fr 23:10 \ft Some ancient translations have Zizah here, which would seem to fit better with v11.\f* Yeush¦197751, and¦197747 Beriah¦197752.
\v 11 (Yahat¦197761 was the¦197762 head¦197762, and¦197763 Zizah¦197763 was second¦197764. Yeush¦197765 and¦197766 Beriah¦197766 were¦197771 \add ≈grouped¦197774 together as one¦197775 family¦197772 unit because they¦197769 didn't¦197767 have¦197769 many¦197769 descendants¦197770\add*.)
\s2 The Kohatites
\rem /s1 Kohathites; The Kohathites
\p
\v 12 Kohat's¦197779 four¦197784 sons¦197778 were¦197780: Amram¦197780, Yitshar¦197781, Hevron¦197782, and¦197783 Uzziel¦197783.
\v 13 Amram's¦197788 sons¦197787 were¦197789 Aharon and¦197790 Mosheh¦197790 \add !(Aaron¦197789 and Moses¦197790)\add*. Aharon \add ≈and his future male descendants¦197798 were permanently appointed\add* to consecrate¦197793 the¦197803 most sacred¦197794 things, to¦197802 burn¦197802 incense¦197802, to minister¦197805 to Yahweh¦197804, and¦197806 to¦197806 bless¦197806 his name¦197807.\x + \xo 23:13: \xt Exo 28:1.\x*
\v 14 Mosheh¦197812 \add was known as\add* \add ≈a man¦197813 who served\add* God¦197814, and¦197812 his¦197815 descendants¦197815 were¦197816 included with the¦197813 \add other\add* Levites¦197820.
\v 15 Mosheh's¦197823 sons¦197822 were¦197824 Gershom¦197824 and¦197825 Eliezer¦197825.
\v 16 Gershom's¦197828 eldest son¦197827 was¦197829 Shevuel¦197829.
\v 17 Eliezer's¦197835 only son¦197833 was Rehavyah, but¦197832 Rehavyah \add went on to\add* have many sons¦197842.
\p
\v 18 Yitshar's¦197850 eldest son¦197849 was¦197851 Shelomot¦197851.
\v 19 Hevron's¦197856 sons¦197855 \add ≈from oldest to youngest\add* were¦197857: Yeriyyah, Amaryah¦197859, Yahaziel¦197861, and¦197863 Yekamean.
\v 20 Uzziel's¦197867 sons¦197866 were¦197868 Mikah¦197868 and¦197870 Yishshiyah¦197870.
\s2 The Merarites
\rem /s1 The Merarites; Merarites
\p
\v 21 Merari's¦197875 sons were¦197876 Mahli¦197879 and Mushi¦197877, \add and\add* Mahli's¦197876 sons¦197878 were¦197880 Eleazar¦197880 and¦197881 Kish¦197881.
\v 22 Eleazar¦197884 died¦197883 without having any sons, \add so\add* his brother Kish's¦197897 sons married¦197894 his daughters¦197893 \add (to continue the family name)\add*.
\v 23 Mushi¦197901 had three¦197905 sons¦197900: Mahli¦197902, Eder¦197903, and¦197903 Yerimot¦197904.
\p
\v 24 Those were¦197908 Levi's¦197910 descendants¦197908 \add ≈by¦197916 their¦197918 clans and¦197927 their appointments, who did the¦197919 work¦197921 of¦197919 serving¦197921 in¦197916 Yahweh's¦197923 residence once they¦197915 reached twenty¦197925 years¦197926 old\add*,
\v 25 because¦197929 David¦197931 had¦197930 said¦197930, “Yisrael's¦197936 god¦197934 Yahweh¦197933 has¦197932 given¦197932 peace to¦197937 his¦197937 people¦197937, and¦197938 he'll \add now\add* live forever¦197942 in¦197939 Yerushalem¦197939,
\v 26 so the Levites¦197945 won't¦197946 need to¦197948 carry¦197948 the¦197951 \add sacred\add* tent¦197951 anymore, along with all¦197954 its¦197956 equipment¦197956.”\x + \xo 23:26: \xt Deu 10:8.\x*
\v 27 \add ≈So one of¦197960 David's¦197961 final¦197962 instructions had been¦197964 to¦197971 count¦197964 the¦197962 Levite¦197967 men who were¦197964 twenty¦197969 years¦197970 old and¦197971 over\add*,
\v 28 because¦197973 their¦197974 work was¦197975 to¦197975 \add ≈assist¦197975\add* Aharon's¦197978 descendants¦197977 in their work in Yahweh's¦197981 residence. They¦197997 \add ≈were¦197975 in charge\add* of the courtyards¦197984 and siderooms, \add ≈in charge of the purification¦197990 ceremonies\add*, and did other work at God's¦197993 residence.\x + \xo 23:28-32: \xt Num 3:5-9.\x*
\v 29 \add ≡They were also¦198001 in charge of\add* the sacred bread, as well as the fine¦198001 flour¦198001 for¦198002 the offering¦198002, the¦198003 wafers¦198003 of¦198003 bread without raising agent, the¦198004 baking pans, and \add ≈all¦198007 the measuring¦198009 and¦198010 mixing of ingredients\add*.
\p
\v 30 Every morning¦198013 and¦198018 every evening¦198019 \add @the Levites\add* stood¦198012 and¦198016 praised¦198016 Yahweh¦198017.
\v 31 They would also¦198027 do that on the rest days, and at¦198028 the new moon¦198026 celebrations and¦198027 during the other religious festivals¦198027. \add ≈There were regulations about how many¦198021 of¦198032 them¦198030 must always be on duty serving\add* Yahweh¦198024.
\v 32 They¦198035 were \add also\add* in charge of¦198038 the sacred¦198044 tent¦198039 and¦198042 the holy¦198044 place¦198044, and¦198045 assisting \add the priests\add* (their relatives¦198048, Aharon's¦198047 descendants¦198046) in their¦198048 service¦198049 at Yahweh's¦198051 residence.
\c 24
