\p
\v 1 Aharon's¦198055 sons¦198057 were¦198059: Nadav¦198059, Avihu¦198060, Eleazar¦198061, and¦198054 Itamar¦198062,
\v 2 \add ≈but¦198064\add* Nadav¦198065 and¦198066 Avihu¦198066 died¦198064 \add ≈before¦198067 their¦198068 father¦198068\add* and¦198069 \add ≈without having any children¦198069, so\add* \add only\add* Eleazar¦198075 and¦198076 Itamar¦198076 became priests¦198074.\x + \xo 24:2: \xt Lev 10:1-2.\x*
\v 3 David¦198079 \add ≈gave Eleazar's¦198084 descendant Tsadok¦198080, and¦198078 Itamar's¦198089 descendant Ahimelek¦198085 two different sets of¦198088 duties¦198090 to¦198090 perform\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈There were¦198093 more¦198100 leaders among Eleazar's descendants than¦198100 there were among Itamar's descendants, so they¦198104 appointed sixteen leaders from Eleazar's descendants and¦198093 eight¦198117 from Itamar's descendants\add*.
\v 5 They¦198119 divided¦198119 up \add ≈the duties by¦198120 a process of¦198128 choosing randomly, so some of¦198131 the¦198132 leaders from¦198133 each of the two groups served the facility and¦198119 others served God directly\add*. DOUBLE-CHECK, along with¦198122 verse 3 as well.
\v 6 Netanel's¦198143 son Shemayah¦198140 was the Levite¦198147 scribe¦198144 who recorded¦198139 all this in¦198148 front¦198148 of¦198148 the¦198149 king¦198149 and¦198150 the¦198150 leaders, Tsadok¦198151 the¦198152 priest¦198152 and¦198153 Abiatar's¦198156 son Ahimelek¦198153, and¦198157 the¦198157 clan leaders of¦198157 the¦198158 priests¦198159 and the Levites¦198147. (One¦198164 family¦198158 from Eleazar's¦198166 group was randomly assigned a duty, and then one¦198145 from Itamar's¦198170 group, and so on.)
\p
\v 7 The¦198174 first¦198175 two \add ≈allocations of duties\add* went¦198173 to¦198176 Yehoyariv¦198176 and¦198173 then Yedayah¦198177.
\v 8 Next were Harim¦198180 and Seorim¦198182,
\v 9 Malkiyah¦198185 and Miyyamin¦198187,
\v 10 Hakkots and Aviyyah,
\v 11 Yeshua¦198195 and Shekanyah¦198197,
\v 12 Elyashiv¦198200 and Yakim¦198203,
\v 13 Huppah¦198207 and Yesheveav,
\v 14 Bilgah¦198214 and Immer¦198217,
\v 15 Hezer and Ha-Pitstsets,
\v 16 Patahyah and Yehezkel¦198231,
\v 17 Yakin¦198234 and¦198236 Gamul¦198237,
\v 18 Delayah and¦198243, lastly, Maazyah¦198244.
\p
\v 19 Those \add were the priests\add* selected to¦198256 \add be leaders of the groups\add* that would serve¦198251 in¦198257 Yahweh's¦198255 temple¦198253, following the instructions¦198261 that Yisrael's¦198264 god¦198263 Yahweh¦198262 had¦198261 given their¦198256 ancestor¦198259 Aharon¦198258.
