\p
\v 1 These were the divisions¦198717 of¦198721 the gatekeepers¦198718:
\li1 From the¦198721 Korahites: Kore's¦198723 son¦198721 Meshelemyah¦198720 (Kore was one¦198724 of Asaf's¦198727 sons¦198726),
\li1
\v 2 Meshelemyah's \add seven\add* sons¦198730 (in order): Zekaryah¦198731, Yediael¦198733, Zebadyah¦198735, Yatniel¦198737,
\v 3 Eylam¦198740, Yehohanan¦198742, and Elyehoenai.
\li1
\v 4 Oved-Edom's \add eight\add* sons¦198749 (in order): Shemayah¦198750, Yehozavad¦198752, Yoah¦198754, Sakar¦198756, Netanel¦198758,\x + \xo 26:4-5: \xt 2Sam 6:11; 1Ch 13:14.\x*
\v 5 Ammiel, Yissakar¦198763, and Peulletai¦198765. (God¦198769 had¦198768 blessed¦198768 him¦198768.)
\li1
\v 6 Oved-Edom's son¦198773 Shemayah¦198772 also¦198772 had sons¦198775. (They¦198783 were leaders¦198776 in their¦198778 father's¦198778 family¦198777 because¦198779 they¦198783 were capable warriors¦198781.)
\v 7 Shemayah's¦198786 sons¦198785 were¦198787: Otni¦198787, Refael¦198788, Oved¦198789, and Elzavad¦198790. His¦198791 relatives¦198791 Elihu¦198795 and¦198796 Semakyah¦198796 were also¦198788 capable men.
