\v 10 Merari's¦198833 descendant¦198831 Hosah's¦198828 sons¦198834: Shimri¦198835 (not¦198838 actually the firstborn¦198841, but¦198828 his¦198843 father¦198843 appointed¦198842 him¦198842 as the first¦198841),
\v 11 Hilkiyah, Tavalyah, and Zekaryah¦198850. (Thirteen sons¦198854 and¦198855 relatives¦198855 in total¦198852.)
\p
\v 12 Those men were leaders¦198863 of the groups¦198861 of men who guarded the temple's gates. They worked in¦198869 Yahweh's¦198870 temple¦198869 like¦198866 their¦198867 relatives¦198867 did.
\v 13 \add ≈They¦198872 used a process of choosing randomly to assign each family to a particular gate¦198878, irrespective of the¦198876 family reputation\add*.
\v 14 Shelemyah's¦198885 group was allocated to the eastern¦198884 gate, and¦198886 his¦198887 son¦198887 Zekaryah¦198886 (a wise adviser) was¦198888 allocated to the northern¦198895 gate.
\v 15 Oved¦198898-Edom's group was allocated to the southern¦198900 gate, plus¦198901 his¦198901 sons¦198901 \add were to guard\add* the storehouses¦198903.
\v 16 Shuppim's¦198905 and¦198906 Hosah's¦198906 groups were allocated the¦198909 western gate¦198909, along¦198914 with the Shalleket¦198910 gate on¦198911 the uphill road¦198911, with \add ≈side-by-side guards¦198913\add*.
\v 17 Every day¦198921 there were six¦198919 Levites¦198918 on duty in the east¦198917, four in the¦198918 north¦198920, four¦198922 in the south¦198923, and¦198926 two¦198927 at the storehouses¦198926.
\v 18 There were four¦198932 on the road¦198933 by the western courtyard, and two¦198934 in the courtyard.
\v 19 Those were¦198938 the¦198938 groups¦198938 of¦198938 men who were Korah's and¦198942 Merari's¦198943 descendants¦198940 who guarded the temple gates.
