\v 26 Shelomot¦199009 and¦199010 his¦199010 relatives¦199010 \add ≈supervised\add* all¦199012 the¦199014 storehouses¦199014 for the¦199015 sacred¦199015 things¦199015 that¦199016 were¦199011 consecrated¦199017 by King¦199019 David¦199018, the \add ≈clan leaders\add*, and the army¦199027 division leaders and other commanders¦199026
\v 27 who'd dedicated some¦199029 of¦199029 the plunder¦199034 \add ≈from¦199032 their battles¦199031\add* to¦199036 the repair¦199036 of¦199037 Yahweh's¦199038 residence.
\v 28 Shelomot and his¦199062 relatives¦199062 were¦199058 also¦199044 in charge of¦199045 everything¦199056 that¦199041 the¦199043 prophet¦199043 Shemuel¦199042, \add King\add* Shaul¦199044 (Kish's¦199047 son), and¦199048 David's two army commanders Abner¦199048 (Ner's¦199051 son) and¦199052 Yoav¦199052 (Tseruyah's¦199055 son) had¦199041 dedicated \add to Yahweh\add*.
