\v 29 From Yitshar's descendants¦199067, Kenanyah¦199066 and¦199067 his¦199067 sons¦199067 worked¦199068 outside¦199069 \add the temple area\add* as officials¦199073 and¦199074 judges¦199074 over¦199070 Yisrael¦199072.
\p
\v 30 From¦199089 Hevron's descendants¦199079, Hashavyah¦199077 and¦199078 his¦199078 relatives¦199078 were¦199086 responsible for all¦199092 the¦199093 work done for Yahweh¦199094 and¦199095 for the king¦199096 in the area west¦199091 of the Yordan¦199090 river. There were 1,700 of them \add ≈who were able to¦199076 do their work well\add*.
\v 31 According to¦199098 the¦199100 records of Hevron's descendants¦199102, Yeriyyah was¦199100 their¦199102 leader¦199100. (In¦199104 the¦199105 fortieth¦199105 year¦199104 of David's¦199107 reign¦199106, they'd¦199108 searched \add ?in those records\add* and¦199109 discovered¦199109 that there were¦199108 powerful¦199111 men in Yazer¦199113 in Gilead¦199114.)
\v 32 \add @Yeriyyah¦199116\add* had 2,700 relatives¦199116 who were¦199117 strong \add workers\add* and¦199121 \add ≈leaders of¦199123 their families¦199124\add*. King¦199127 David¦199126 \add ≈put them in charge¦199125 of governing\add* the tribes¦199133 of Reuven, Gad, and the eastern half¦199132 of the tribe¦199133 of¦199133 Menashsheh, \add ≈to¦199135 ensure that all¦199135 the people did what God commanded and¦199139 what the king¦199140 told them to do\add*.
