\c 28
\s1 David's temple plans
\rem /s1 Solomon Instructed to Build the Temple; David's Instructions for the Temple; David's Plans for the Temple; David's Instructions to Solomon
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* David¦199668 called all¦199671 of Yisrael's¦199674 leaders to assemble¦199667 in Yerushalem¦199706: the tribal leaders, the leaders of the \add various\add* divisions¦199678 that¦199679 served¦199679 the¦199682 king¦199682, the¦199683 commanders¦199683 of army units of thousands¦199684 and¦199685 of¦199685 hundreds¦199686, and¦199687 the¦199687 supervisors of¦199687 all¦199688 the¦199690 property¦199690 and¦199692 cattle belonging to¦199694 the¦199694 king¦199694 and¦199695 his¦199695 sons¦199695, along with¦199696 the¦199698 top officials¦199698, and¦199699 the¦199699 warriors¦199699, including¦199667 \add ≈their powerful¦199702 heroes\add*.
\p
\v 2 Then¦199708 King¦199710 David¦199709 stood up¦199708 and¦199714 spoke¦199714, “Listen¦199715 to¦199715 me¦199715, my¦199716 brothers¦199716 and¦199717 my people¦199717, I¦199718 wanted in my heart¦199721 to¦199722 put up a¦199723 building for¦199725 the¦199725 box¦199725 containing Yahweh's¦199728 agreement¦199726 to rest¦199724 in. It's¦199708 the footstool¦199729 for our¦199731 god's¦199731 feet¦199713, and I've made preparations¦199732 to¦199733 start building¦199733,\x + \xo 28:2-7: \xt 2Sam 7:1-16; 1Ch 17:1-14.\x*
\v 3 but¦199735 God¦199735 told¦199736 me¦199737 that I wouldn't be the¦199735 one to¦199737 build¦199740 a house¦199741 to \add ≈honour him\add*, because¦199743 I've \add ≈been involved in a lot of¦199742 war¦199745 and¦199747 killings\add*.
\p
\v 4 “Yet Yisrael's¦199763 god¦199752 Yahweh¦199751 chose¦199750 me¦199754 from¦199755 all¦199755 of¦199756 my¦199758 father's¦199758 family to¦199759 be¦199759 king¦199760 over¦199761 Yisrael forever¦199764, because¦199765 he¦199767 chose¦199767 a leader¦199768 from \add the tribe of\add* Yehudah¦199766, my father's tribe, and¦199750 among¦199773 my father's sons¦199773, he was¦199759 pleased¦199776 to¦199777 make¦199777 me king over all of Yisrael¦199753.
\v 5 Then¦199784 out of the many¦199788 sons¦199789 that he's¦199790 given¦199790 me¦199791, he¦199793 chose¦199793 my¦199795 son¦199795 Shelomoh¦199794 \add !(Solomon¦199794)\add* to¦199796 \add ≈be the next king¦199800 to rule his kingdom¦199800 of¦199800\add* Yisrael¦199804.
\p
\v 6 “Then¦199806 he¦199806 told¦199806 me¦199807, ‘Your¦199821 son Shelomoh¦199808 is the one who'll build¦199812 my temple¦199813 and¦199814 the courtyards¦199814 \add around it\add*, because¦199815 I've¦199817 chosen¦199817 him¦199818 to be like my son¦199820, and¦199821 I'll¦199822 be like a father¦199825 to him.
\v 7 I'll¦199827 establish¦199827 his¦199830 kingdom¦199830 forever¦199833, if¦199834 he's¦199836 diligent at following my instructions¦199838 and¦199827 \add obeying\add* my¦199838 judgements¦199839, like he¦199836 is¦199836 at present.’
\p
\v 8 “\add ≈So¦199843\add* now¦199843, in \add ≈front\add* of¦199844 all¦199845 of¦199845 Yisrael¦199847, Yahweh's¦199850 assembly¦199848, and¦199851 in¦199851 the¦199851 hearing¦199851 of¦199851 our¦199852 god¦199852, \add I challenge you all to discover and obey\add* all¦199855 of¦199855 your god Yahweh's commands¦199857, so¦199860 that¦199860 you'll all possess¦199861 the good¦199865 land¦199864, and¦199866 you'll leave¦199866 your sons after¦199868 you to inherit¦199866 it forever¦199871.
\p
\v 9 “And¦199874 you, Shelomoh¦199875 my¦199877 son¦199877, \add ≈follow\add* your¦199882 father's¦199882 god¦199881 and¦199883 serve¦199883 him¦199883 with¦199884 a whole¦199889 heart¦199884 and¦199886 with¦199886 a willing¦199887 life, because¦199888 Yahweh¦199893 \add ≈looks into\add* all hearts¦199891, and¦199894 understands¦199898 all \add ≈your motives\add*. If¦199899 you look¦199892 for¦199903 him, he'll \add make sure\add* you find¦199902 him, but¦199874 if¦199904 you¦199906 abandon¦199906 him¦199906, he'll reject¦199907 you¦199907 forever¦199908.
\v 10 You¦199917 can now¦199912 see¦199910 that you need to be¦199922 strong¦199922 and¦199923 get busy, because¦199913 Yahweh¦199915 has¦199916 chosen¦199916 you to erect a building¦199918 to be his sanctuary¦199921.”
\p
\v 11 Then David¦199927 gave¦199926 the plans for \add the temple\add* to¦199928 his¦199929 son¦199929 Shelomoh¦199928, \add including plans\add* for its porch¦199933, its houses¦199936, its¦199936 treasuries¦199937, its upper¦199938 rooms¦199938 and¦199939 its¦199939 inner¦199940 rooms, and¦199941 the¦199941 \add ≈room to contain the¦199942 sacred box\add*.
\v 12 \add He also handed over\add* the¦199944 plans he envisioned for¦199950 the¦199950 temple courtyards¦199950, all¦199954 the¦199956 surrounding¦199957 apartments, all the treasuries, and¦199944 all the storerooms¦199958 for¦199961 sacred¦199962 things¦199962.
\v 13 \add He included instructions\add* for¦199964 the¦199964 divisions¦199964 of¦199964 the¦199965 priests¦199965 and¦199966 Levites¦199966, for all¦199967 the \add ≈services¦199970 required to¦199967 operate the temple, and¦199974 for¦199974 all¦199974 the¦199976 equipment¦199976 and utensils¦199976 needed for all that\add*.
\v 14 \add David had determined\add* the weight¦199983 of¦199991 gold¦199984 and¦199989 silver¦199992 that would be needed to¦199990 make all¦199990 the necessary items that would be used in¦199983 the regular temple functions,
\v 15 \add including\add* the gold¦200002 lampstands and lamps¦200009 and¦200010 the silver¦200011 lampstands¦200013 and¦200014 lamps¦200014,
\v 16 and¦200019 the¦200021 gold¦200021 for¦200023 the¦200023 display tables¦200023, and the silver¦200027 for¦200028 the silver tables.
\v 17 \add ≈Also¦200031\add* the pure¦200035 gold meat forks¦200031 and the jugs¦200033 and basins¦200032, and the weights of¦200036 the¦200037 gold¦200037 and silver¦200042 bowls¦200041.
\v 18 Then¦200047 the weight¦200051 of refined¦200050 gold¦200049 for the incense¦200048 altar¦200047, and¦200047 for¦200047 making the winged creatures that¦200056 spread¦200056 out¦200056 across¦200058 the top of the box¦200060 \add ≈containing\add* Yahweh's¦200063 agreement¦200061.
\v 19 \add He said\add*, “I've written¦200066 down all¦200071 those plans \add ≈following Yahweh's¦200068 direction, as he¦200070 gave me¦200069 instructions for what has to be done\add*.”
\v 20 Then David¦200077 told¦200076 his¦200079 son¦200079 Shelomoh¦200078, “Be¦200080 strong¦200080 and¦200081 courageous¦200081, and¦200082 \add ≈get going\add*. Don't¦200083 be¦200085 afraid¦200085 or discouraged¦200088, because¦200089 Yahweh¦200107 God¦200091, my¦200092 god¦200091, is¦200093 with¦200093 you¦200093. He¦200095 won't leave you¦200095 and he¦200097 won't abandon¦200097 you¦200097 before¦200098 all¦200101 the work¦200104 of¦200103 \add ≈constructing\add* Yahweh's¦200090 residence \add ≈and the necessary equipment\add* is¦200100 finished¦200100.
\v 21 Listen, the¦200110 divisions¦200110 of¦200110 the¦200111 priests¦200111 and¦200112 the¦200112 Levites¦200112 for all¦200113 the work in God's house¦200116, and¦200118 all¦200119 the¦200121 \add ≈skilled¦200125 workmen, will¦200118 be¦200118 backing you¦200118 in¦200119 all the work¦200115\add*. The¦200129 officials¦200129 and¦200130 all¦200130 the¦200132 people¦200132 are¦200118 \add ≈ready to¦200133 follow your¦200135 instructions\add*.”
\c 29
\s1 Donations for the temple
\rem /s1 Gifts for Building the Temple; Solomon succeeds David as king; Offerings for Building the Temple
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 1 Then King¦200140 David¦200139 told¦200138 the entire assembly¦200143, “My¦200145 son¦200145 Shelomoh¦200144 \add !(Solomon¦200144)\add* \add ≈has¦200147 been chosen¦200147 by God himself\add*. He's¦200138 young¦200145 and tender, and \add ≈it's¦200138 a¦200151 huge¦200154 job\add*, because¦200155 the¦200158 temple¦200158 isn't¦200156 being built for people, but¦200138 for Yahweh¦200160 God¦200161.\x + \xo 29:1-2: \xt 1Ch 22:5.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈I've¦200166 used all my resources to¦200163 provide a plentiful supply of¦200163 materials\add* for¦200167 my¦200169 god's¦200169 residence: the¦200170 gold¦200170 for¦200172 the gold¦200172 things, and¦200173 the¦200173 silver¦200173 for¦200174 the silver¦200174 things, the¦200175 bronze¦200175 for¦200176 the bronze¦200176 things, the¦200177 iron¦200177 for¦200178 the iron¦200178 things, the¦200179 wood for¦200180 the wooden parts, onyx¦200183 stones¦200185 for inlays, antimony¦200187 stones and¦200188 colourful¦200188 things, and¦200189 all¦200189 the rare stones¦200190, and¦200192 alabaster¦200194 stones.
\v 3 What's more, because¦200198 I'm excited to¦200203 have¦200214 my god's¦200210 residence \add built\add*, I've donated my own personal gold¦200205 and¦200206 silver¦200206 on¦200198 top of¦200210 everything else that¦200214 I've prepared¦200214 for¦200215 the¦200208 sacred¦200216 temple:
\v 4 100 tonnes of gold¦200221 and¦200224 2,500 tonnes of refined¦200229 silver¦200228 for overlaying¦200230 the¦200231 buildings' walls¦200231,
\v 5 \add as well as\add* gold¦200234 for¦200235 the gold¦200235 things, silver¦200236 for¦200237 the silver¦200237 things, and¦200238 for¦200238 everything the¦200241 craftsmen¦200242 \add ≈are¦200244 going to make¦200244\add*. \add ≈So\add* who's¦200243 willing \add ≈to commit themselves\add* today to making¦200244 a contribution¦200244 towards Yahweh's¦200248 work¦200240?
\p
\v 6 Then¦200256 the family¦200252 leaders and¦200253 the¦200253 leaders¦200253 of¦200253 the¦200255 \add ≈tribes¦200255\add*, and¦200257 the¦200257 \add ≈various levels of military\add* commanders¦200257, and the king's¦200262 \add ≈construction overseers\add*, \add all\add* contributed¦200250 willingly¦200250.
\v 7 They¦200268 donated \add a total of\add* 170 tonnes of gold and 100kg of gold coins, 350 tonnes of silver¦200276, 600 tonnes of¦200278 bronze¦200280, and¦200282 3,400 tonnes of¦200282 iron¦200285 for¦200265 the¦200265 \add ≈temple¦200266\add* construction,
\v 8 plus anyone¦200291 who¦200291 had precious stones¦200293 donated them¦200294 to¦200295 the¦200295 treasury¦200295 for the¦200296 \add ≈temple¦200296\add*. Yehiel¦200302 (a Gershonite) \add ≈was¦200294 in¦200294 charge¦200294 of¦200294 those¦200294\add*.
\v 9 The¦200306 people¦200306 were \add ≈excited\add*, because¦200307 they'd¦200313 \add all\add* given¦200309 willingly¦200309 to¦200314 Yahweh¦200314, and¦200315 King¦200317 David¦200316 was also¦200315 very pleased.
\s1 The praying for David
\rem /s1 David's Prayer of Praise; David's Praise to God; David Praises God; David's Prayer
\s4 Full kingdom
\p
\v 10 Then \add King\add* David¦200324 blessed¦200323 Yahweh in \add ≈front of¦200328\add* the¦200331 entire¦200329 assembly¦200331, saying¦200332, “You¦200335 are¦200334 blessed¦200334, Yahweh, Yisrael's¦200338 god¦200337, our¦200339 father¦200339, \add ≈for all¦200329 time, both past and¦200341 future\add*.
\v 11 Greatness¦200347, power¦200348, beauty, splendour¦200349, and majesty¦200351 \add all belong\add* to you, Yahweh, as indeed does everything¦200354 in¦200355 the heavens¦200355 and on¦200355 the earth¦200356. The¦200349 kingdom¦200359 and¦200360 \add ≈supreme leadership\add* \add all belong\add* to you, Yahweh.\x + \xo 29:11: \xt Mat 6:13.\x*
\v 12 Wealth¦200365 and \add prestige comes from you\add*, and you¦200367 rule¦200369 over¦200370 everything¦200370. \add ≈You¦200367 have the¦200365 power¦200372 and¦200373 strength¦200373 and¦200374 control\add* to¦200375 make¦200375 \add people\add* great¦200375 and to strengthen¦200373 everyone¦200377,
\v 13 \add ≈so\add* now¦200379, our¦200380 god¦200380, we're¦200384 thanking¦200381 you and¦200379 praising¦200384 your¦200386 beautiful name¦200385.
\p
\v 14 But¦200388 who¦200389 am¦200390 I¦200390, and¦200391 who¦200391 are¦200392 my¦200392 people¦200392, that¦200398 we should \add ≈be in a position to be able\add* to donate freely like¦200398 this¦200398? \add ≈Yes,\add* everything¦200402 comes from you, and \add ≈we've¦200404 simply given¦200404 back from what you gave¦200404 to¦200405 us\add*,
\v 15 because¦200407 we're \add just\add* strangers on the earth \add ≈in your¦200411 eyes\add*, and¦200412 foreign guests, like¦200413 all¦200413 our¦200415 ancestors¦200415. Our¦200418 time¦200418 on¦200419 the¦200421 earth¦200421 is¦200422 like a shadow¦200416 \add ≈without any permanence\add*.
\v 16 Yahweh¦200425 our¦200426 god¦200426, all¦200427 this¦200429 abundance¦200428 that¦200430 we've¦200431 \add ≈collected\add* in order to¦200432 build¦200432 a house¦200435 for you, for your¦200438 holy name¦200436, \add ≈originally came from¦200438 you, and¦200441 it¦200439 all belongs¦200441 to¦200441 you¦200441\add* \add anyway\add*.
\v 17 \add ≈Yes\add* I know¦200444, my¦200445 god¦200445, that¦200446 you¦200447 examine our hearts¦200449, and you're¦200447 pleased¦200451 \add ≈when we do what's right\add*. I've¦200455 freely offered all¦200456 these¦200458 \add gifts\add* \add ≈as I strive to do what's right\add*, and¦200459 now¦200459 \add ≈I'm also¦200450 happy to\add* see¦200464 your¦200460 people¦200460 freely offer \add gifts\add* to you.
\v 18 Yahweh¦200470, god¦200471 of¦200471 our¦200475 ancestors¦200475 Abraham¦200472, Yitshak¦200473 \add !(Isaac¦200473)\add*, and¦200474 Yisrael¦200474 \add !(Israel¦200474)\add*, \add help your people continue to desire to do things like this forever, and help them remain loyal to you\add*.
